MenuCommand <p>In Group <code>&lt;group&gt;</code>:</p> <ul> <li>Rename: type the new name in chat.</li> <li>Delete group: confirm. The doors are kept; triggers targeting the group are removed.</li> </ul> <pre><code>/dp group rename &lt;group&gt; &lt;name&gt;
/dp group delete &lt;group&gt;
</code></pre>

Key Type Default Effect <code>sounds.enabled</code> <code>true</code>/<code>false</code> <code>true</code> <code>false</code> silences every door sound. <code>sounds.&lt;type&gt;.start</code> sound depends on type Played when the door starts moving. <code>sounds.&lt;type&gt;.loop</code> sound depends on type Repeated while the door moves, every <code>interval-ticks</code>. <code>sounds.&lt;type&gt;.end</code> sound depends on type Played when the door stops. <p>Each sound has these fields:</p> Field Default Allowed values Effect <code>sound</code> a vanilla sound key, for example <code>'minecraft:block.piston.extend'</code>; <code>''</code> = no sound Sound to play. Only vanilla sounds are supported. The name is not checked: a misspelled name is simply not heard. <code>volume</code> <code>1.0</code> <code>0</code> or more Volume. Larger values are heard from farther away. <code>pitch</code> <code>1.0</code> <code>0.5</code> to <code>2.0</code> (values outside are clamped) Pitch. <code>interval-ticks</code> <code>10</code> <code>1</code> or more Loop sounds only: time between repetitions. <p>Example, a quieter drawbridge without the loop sound:</p> <pre><code>sounds:
  drawbridge:
    start: { sound: 'minecraft:block.chain.break', volume: 0.6, pitch: 0.6 }
    loop:  { sound: '', volume: 0.0, pitch: 1.0, interval-ticks: 8 }
    end:   { sound: 'minecraft:block.wood.place', volume: 0.6, pitch: 0.5 }
</code></pre> <p>The default sounds of every type are in the <code>config.yml</code> generated on first start.</p>
